// BUGGY spend-cap policy — sums over Transfer::response rows only (settled
// completions). In-flight (issued, not-yet-responded) transfers are invisible
// to the sum, so a parallel burst of fires can overshoot the 200 cap.
//
// The one-word bug: `response` instead of `request`.
//
// Schema: Drupe namespace (alert_total_transfer_over_200 schema).
// TransferInput carries `amount: Long`; TransferOutput is empty.
// The response event carries the same `input` as its request, so
// `response{ input.amount: a }` is well-formed.
//
// Counterexample (parallel-fire race):
//   fire(amount=100) -> permit  (sum=0,  0+100<=200)
//   fire(amount=100) -> permit  (sum=0,  0+100<=200)   <-- response not yet arrived
//   fire(amount=100) -> permit  (sum=0,  0+100<=200)   <-- 3 in-flight, committed=300>200
//
// See: examples/refund_budget_settled_plus_current/policy.dw (the `response`-sum idiom).
// Spec: guide/08-formal-specification.md §6 — evaluation at position i reads only
//   positions j <= i, including the current event; §6.1 — observe-before-decide.
//   + guide/04 (04-temporal-expressions.md) "Evaluation semantics" — decision at
//   timepoint i reads history 0..=i (current event included); windows closed/inclusive.

@id("spendcap_buggy")
permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Transfer",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    (sum a for (a: Long), (t: Timepoint). where (
        formerly within 24h (Drupe::Action::"Transfer"::response{ input.amount: a } && tp(t))
    )) <= 200
};
